      <div type="edition" n="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0445.adelon_dramaton.kock1888-grc1" xml:lang="grc" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0445_adelon_dramaton">
        <head>ΑΔΗΛΩΝ ΔΡΑΜΑΤΩΝ</head>
        <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="1" xml:id="kock-0445-adelon_dramaton-1" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0445_adelon_dramaton">
          <note type="apparatus">Fr. 1 vel post ea quae disputaverunt Herwerdenus 190 et O. Crusius p. 622. 3 non magis intellego quam antea.</note>
        </div>
        <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="2" xml:id="kock-0445-adelon_dramaton-2" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0445_adelon_dramaton">
          <note type="apparatus">2, 11 ὡς γὰρ στρατηγός nunc etiam Madvig. Adv. crit. III 64. — 28 ὅσ’ ἔνεστι καταγεγρ. Ellis Amer. Journ. VI 6, cuius reliquae coniecturae admitti vix possunt. neque magis vero ea quae Madvigius proponit Advers. crit. III 64. — 37 scr. ἔφησθ’ ἔχοντα. Nauck. Bullet. Petersb. XII 514.</note>
        </div>
        <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="4" xml:id="kock-0445-adelon_dramaton-4" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0445_adelon_dramaton">
          <note type="apparatus">4, 4. ταχὺν ὄντα hic nihil aliud significat quam ubique: ‘cum homo velox sit’. quod cur sententiae minus aptum iudicet Herwerd. 190 non exputo.</note>
        </div>
        <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="5" xml:id="kock-0445-adelon_dramaton-5" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0445_adelon_dramaton">
          <note type="apparatus">5, 2. del. verba ‘fortasse κύμβαι’. cf. v. 3.</note>
        </div>
        <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="10" xml:id="kock-0445-adelon_dramaton-10" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0445_adelon_dramaton">
          <note type="apparatus">10. monost. 43 αὐτὸς πενόμενος. — ceterum de hoc et de fr. 7 cf. Dionys. trag. 7. 8 N.</note>
        </div>
      </div>
    </body>
